        ('How much sleep do I need if I train hard?', 'Adults are commonly advised to get 7 to 9 hours a night. Needs are individual, so treat it as a range. If you wake up rested and stay alert during the day, you are probably close to your number. Regularly sleeping under 7 hours usually hurts strength and recovery.'),
